text:
WHAT a wretched world is this:
w Floods and famine and despair;
Little right, but much amiss,


Trouble breeding everywhere;
Tainted food and poisoned wells,


Fickle friends and haunting fear
When your tummy-tum rebels


And your liver's out of gear.
EFFORTS useless, hope is vain;
II An the great things have been done;
Sin and sorrow, sickness, pain,


Many cares and little fun;
Rogues a-plenty, honest men


Listed for misfortune's frown;
Everywhere injustice-when


Indigestion has you down.
MAYNARD children, faithless wives,
w Vice and vanity and greed;
Foolish faith and wasted lives,


All the gardens gone to seed;


Evils in an endless brood,


Envy, jealousy and hate
When you've filled yourself with food


That you can't assimilate.
NOTHING'S lovely; ugliness
~ Looms wherever you may look;
Others keep you from success,


Beating you by hook or crook;
All the world is off the track,


Brown spots float before your eyes
When you eat too much and lack


Necessary exercise.

