text:
COME men have luck that others lack;
~ Some till the soil, some sail the seas;
Some men are doomed to walk the track,


Some ride in splendor and at ease;
Some men must labor long and late,


Mstreated or misunderstood,
And having cause to mourn their fate:


We can't all live at Hollywood.
COME men are we'll and some are i'll;
~ Some men win fame, some die unknown;
Some men go stumbling down the hill,


Some find each rock a stepping stone;
Some men must work, while others play,
Some practice patience, as they should
And some are weary of delay:


We can't all live at Hollywood.
GONE men reach Carcassonne, and ssme
- It's wonders never may behold;
To some men easy fortunes come,


Some sit neglected, bent and old;
Some men are bold and some are meek,


Some win where others never could;
Some men must miss the goals they seek:


We can't all live at Hollywood.
GONE men may sip the sweets of life;
y For some the bitter dregs are poured;
Some struggle through unceasing strife,


Denied the chance to be Ford;
Some men aspire to this or that,


Some preach the creed of brotherhood,
But, long or short, or lean or fat,


We can't all live at Hollywood.

TUNE, alas, Is flying fast;
i Weeks and months and seasons fade;
Five years since they marched us past


Those who watched the big parade.
Senator and governor,


Standing where the flags were bright,
Cheered us As we trudged along;
Everybody for us strong.


Tears Of wonder and delight!
LIVE years since that summer day!
Il One was somewhere In the crowd,
Filled with fear, and bent and gray,


Praying silently-and proud!
Portly Judge and millionaire


Wiped away their manly tears;
Clearly ] remember yet,
But II seems that they forget;


Changes come with changing years.
CHE who saw no one but me
- Marching In the heat and dust
Sleeps beside inland sea;


God, I hope, rewards her trust
Five years since the order came,


Quick entraining In the night;
Mystery and hope and doubt,
Then the fateful moving out


Times sees changes In Its flight
LIVE years, and the fear Is past;
IL Those who cheered have ceased to cheer;
Where the skies were overcast


All is bright again and clear;
Senator and governor,


Portly Judge and millionaire
Stand no more where bugiers blow;
Fast the seasons come and go


Where's that bonus, boys, oh, wheref

