text:
THINGS aren't always going wrong,
i They turn out often they should;
Not all the wicked men strong,


And there are strong men who arc good;
Sometimes plans not upset;
Some picnic parties don't get wet.
COME men, though married have been glad,
- Some wives are truly satisfied;
We open more good eggs than bad,


Worth isn't always pushed aside;
The girls don't always answer no,
And there are fountain pens that flow.
4 RT Is not always fed crusts,
n The doctors pull some patients through;
He Is not always duped who trusts,


And often honest hope comes true;
Faith shames the devil and his works;
There are some civil ticket clerks.
WE do not always wait In vain
w For promises TO be fulfilled;
There's laughter still, despite the pain;


Sometimes the beans remain unspilled;
And canteloupes sometimes are good.
AIOT all Is wrong, and much Is right;
~ The false has not crushed out the true;
Love still prevails in spite Of spite,


The rogues who win respectl are few;
The prospects frequently are fair,
And twins continue to be rare.

